      "satisfier": "originating-requester",
      "text": "Changes requested: pure checkpoint DATA producer with owned-input repair, at exact head 5bf6ccda36e2d83a372fec4f2579d22adce466e0 (repaired producer 13e777b0, base 1db5e12f, 205 paths in 19 artifacts). The production code is approved in substance. One test-harness defect must be fixed before landing (H-1), because the same class of defect already broke main's full suite once (N-1, 54436131).\n\nProduction (read in full):\n- native-checkpoint-producer.ts:\n  - The owned-input repair is right. The brand is checked through the captured intrinsic typed-array toStringTag getter, and the length through the intrinsic length getter, before allocation; caps are checked before the copy; the copy uses the captured Uint8Array.prototype.set. No caller length, buffer, slice, species, constructor or iterator is ever dispatched. A Proxy or fake view yields no 'Uint8Array' tag and is refused.\n  - Each row array's length is read once as a safe non-negative integer, excluding -0, and charged before capture. Elements are read only through data descriptors, so there are no getters.\n  - The header fields are canonicalised once into an owned copy. Everything is captured synchronously before the first await.\n  - Production reuses the existing closed readers (readCheckpointPage, readCompleteCheckpointTable, deriveCheckpointIndexes, readCheckpointAssertion) on its own output.\n  - Greedy 128 KiB pages are built from whole canonical rows, a single over-size row is refused, and empty tables produce no pages.\n  - Payloads are split into 32 KiB byteChunk records plus a byteManifest. The inventory is deduplicated by CID within 100,000 records and 48 MiB, and records are sorted by path.\n  - Frontier and stall coherence with the supplied history are checked. Selective outcomes are validated and then exported as null; only a complete 1..frontier set becomes a table.\n  - It is DATA only, with no publication, generation, archive closure or truth claim.\n- checkpoint-data.ts gains readCheckpointAssertion: a closed 15-field reader with scope, frontier/head ordering and stall-boundary checks.\n- Neither module is reachable from a supported barrel.\n\nWhat I ran, in a clean clone at the full SHA (npm ci and build, Node 26.10.0, real Chromium):\n- npm run check passed.\n- Full npm test: 547 of 547 passed.\n- Focused run of the four new test files with --test-concurrency=1: 3 of 4 passed. tests/native-checkpoint-producer-browser.test.ts failed with ENOENT opening .atseq-local/native-checkpoint-producer/browser-bundle.js.\n- I read the owned-input corpus (alias-then-mutate, no dispatch of caller methods, subclass copy, ownership before await, row count read once, foreign getter identity). It covers the reported defect 57d67561.\n\nH-1 (required, test only): the Chromium producer test writes into a directory created by another test.\n- Line 13 calls mkdir('.atseq-local', { recursive: true }), but line 37 writes .atseq-local/native-checkpoint-producer/browser-bundle.js, and line 83 writes browser.json there.\n- That subdirectory exists only if a sibling test has already created it. The test passes in the full suite only because of ordering, and it fails when run alone or first.\n- Fix: mkdir('.atseq-local/native-checkpoint-producer', { recursive: true }). Better still, write under the capture directory the test already owns. Then confirm the browser test passes alone from a clean .atseq-local.\n- Please also check the owned-input browser test for the same pattern.\n\nOnce H-1 is fixed I expect to approve without further production review. Full P3/P4, archive and publication closure, and generation joins remain open, and all 106 original vectors remain UNEXECUTED, as stated.",
